ay the concept  actually only came up a couple of weeks  before filming and was inspired by an  entirely different production altogether  back when the mobius actor was filming a  project called documentary now  he went through loads of different wigs  one in particular that was  very similar to the hair he has in the  loki series while the wig didn't end up  being used for that project  wilson was a really big fan of the look  and when it came time to take to the mcu  screen  the actor suggested it to the team as a  possible look  the crew said yes and gray-haired mobius  was born  according to wilson the look really  embodies the character  so much so that he and the team have a  hard time imagining mobius looking any  other way  honestly we agree it's the perfect look  for the character  you betrayed me you betrayed me oh grow  up grow up  it isn't just the lead characters that  go through different makeup wig and  costume options to find the perfect look  even smaller day player roles like the  flight attendant actress erica coleman  she went through a much more rigorous  costume experience than we would expect  pullman actually had about four or five  fittings for that one costume alone  which doesn't even get a huge amount of  screen time  is there anything else i can do for you  sir i suppose we'll find out won't we  in an interview the actress shared that  her outfit was in fact  custom made for her this is often the  case across the board  in the mcu there is no shortage of time  work and effort put into every detail of  the production  what kind of detail are we talking about  well coleman said that the adjustments  varied from small things like how high  the neckline should go  to where different pockets should be and  even how many buttons should be attached  the detailed work doesn't just apply to  what we see on the actors though  consideration is put into what actors  wear under their costumes as well  coleman was actually given undergarments  to suit the appropriate time period  we bet she was probably pretty surprised  when she was handed 70s style underwear  by the costume department  as for makeup coleman's stewardess  doesn't seem too complex but that didn't  mean  she wasn't given half a dozen options of  red lipstick to try  in order to find the absolute best tone  of red that would match her outfit and  complete the image  this type of detailed work plays a major  part in establishing these worlds of the  mcu  see you again someday  if this series has shown us anything  it's that there are  in fact loads of loki's which one of us  are you  so how do they compare to the different  iterations of the comics  we've got richard e grant as classic  loki rocking the classic suit that we  all know  he's overly sensitive like the rest of  us the last time we saw this style of  outfit was actually in the halloween  episode of wandavision  when vision appeared wearing a very  similar looking costume  kid loki played by jack veal is part of  the classic loki crew from the comics  appearing in journey into mystery and  young avengers comics  his style is pretty similar to classic  loki we can somewhat see the evolution  from kid to classic between the two  what was your nexus event your majesty i  killed ball  boastful loki aka deobia operae  stands out from all the other loki's in  this darker outfit  while this variant loki prefers to be  called sylvie since loki isn't who she  is anymore  her look in the comics and series are  pretty similar  especially compared to what tom  hiddleston's loki is dressed like  small details on the outfits like the  woven black leather and gold accent on  the chest  make it clear there is a definite  connection it's impressive to see just  how  many details and references the team  manages to include  there's no need to be dramatic but yeah  kind of the mcu has managed to make both  impressive and innovative costumes for  the series  demonstrating just how much goes into  costuming 